houritsu: licence, credit and source

What is not copyrighted

The statute text in this repository is not copyrighted (Copyright Act of Japan, Article
13; 著作権法第13条), and neither is its mechanical conversion to markdown. You may use
them without permission. The licence below adds no restriction on using them.

Licence

Whatever in this repository the author (Kohei-Wada) holds copyright or other licensable
rights in is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
The licence applies to nothing else.

Credit

If you reuse the data, a credit to houritsu (https://github.com/Kohei-Wada/houritsu) is
appreciated. Where no licence is needed, this is a request, not a requirement.

Source

This section states where the data comes from and what was changed. It is separate from
the licence terms above.

Source: e-Gov法令検索 (https://laws.e-gov.go.jp/), Public Data License 1.0
(https://www.digital.go.jp/resources/open_data/public_data_license_v1.0). Edited into
markdown by houritsu-builder (Kohei-Wada): the characters of the statute text are
unchanged; headings, markdown escapes and figure links are added. Bill numbers and links
to bill pages come from the bill database by smartnews-smri
(https://github.com/smartnews-smri/house-of-representatives, MIT).

No warranty

This is not legal advice, and the text may be out of date or wrong. It is not the
official text; the official text is the 官報. Check e-Gov or the 官報 before relying on
it.
